      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #61617\n\n`_build_fa_remote()` looks up the full-attention KV group index with a\nbare `next(...)`, which raises `StopIteration` for models without any\nattention group (SSM-only, e.g. Mamba models). The exception aborts the\nwhole NIXL handshake and every subsequent transfer fails with an\nunhelpful `handshake_failed`.\n\nThe same bare lookup also exists in `_build_local_splits_from_plan()`\n(heterogeneous-TP path).\n\n## Fix\n\n- `_build_fa_remote()`: when no attention group exists, fall back to the\n  sole non-attention group's source ranks. FA descriptors are still\n  emitted: on SSM-only models those slots are layout padding that the\n  producer registers (`_build_fa_local`) and that `_compute_desc_ids`\n  offsets SSM descriptor ids past, so they must exist for the read index\n  math to stay aligned.\n- `_build_local_splits_from_plan()`: same fallback for the FA split\n  count.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n- Added unit tests for both functions with SSM-only spec types.\n- End-to-end verified on GPU (A100, NIXL/UCX pull mode, P+D disagg\n  serving state-spaces/mamba-130m, homogeneous TP1):\n  - before the patch: the decode-side handshake dies with\n    `StopIteration`;\n  - with the patch applied to the same setup: handshake, KV transfer\n    and remote decode all succeed (1 successful transfer, 48\n    descriptors, ~1.3 MB, ~23 ms; the decode completes the prompt\n    correctly with 0 transfer failures in the logs).",
